  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday morning through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 153 PM EDT Wed Jun 24 2026\n\nTo begin the period, a H500 ridge will be centered just west of the \nstate over MS/LA. Given the strong ridge of high pressure, calm and \ndry conditions are expected through much of the period. With that \nsaid, dangerously hot temperatures and heat index values are \nexpected. \n\nSome low end PoPs are possible underneath this ridge but the main \nhazard will be the hot and humid conditions leading to dangerous \nheat index values this weekend and into early next week.\n\nTemperatures are expected to be above average as high pressure \ncenters itself just west of the state. Max heat index values will \nlikely get into the upper 90s to just over 100 degrees across much \nof the state by this weekend and into early next week.",
